{title: Herren er min hyrde}
{subtitle: Psalm 23}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] |
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The LORD is my shepherd, I [Eb]lack nothing
He [Gm]lets me lie down in green [Eb]pastures
[Gm]He leads me beside still [Eb]waters
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]He re[F]stores my [Eb]soul
He guides me along right paths
[Gm]For his name's sake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Even though I walk through the valley [Eb]of the shadows
I [Gm]fear no evil, for you [Eb]are with me
Your [Gm]rod and your [F]staff, they comfort [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Gm] | [F] | ×2
| [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm]You set a table [F]before me in the pre[Eb]sence of my enemies
[Gm]You anoint my [F]head with oil, my [Eb]cup overflows
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Surely [Gm]goodness and mer[F]cy will pursue [Eb]me all the days of my [Gm]life
And I will [Eb]dwell in the [F]house of the [Eb]LORD for length of [Gm]days
{end_of_verse}

